{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2458","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2458","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2458\",\"parent_revision\":\"2d6cc40b0e92a6333b00e3f6556964afa086161e8ce5765e37e8fd8230b7c5d3\",\"root_revision\":\"2d6cc40b0e92a6333b00e3f6556964afa086161e8ce5765e37e8fd8230b7c5d3\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe Recursive Follow-up Handling step in `complete-implementation` calls `artifact_read(item_id, artifact_type=\\\"codebase-analysis\\\")` to obtain the code review verdict. The call returned `{\\\"error\\\": \\\"No artifacts of type 'codebase-analysis' found for item #2437\\\"}`. `artifact_list(2437)` showed the `dh:code-reviewer` agent had registered its output as `artifact_type=\\\"audit-report\\\"` with `artifact_id=\\\"code-review-2437-T1\\\"`. Reading the `audit-report` artifact returned the expected verdict field.\\n\\nThe artifact type name in the skill (`codebase-analysis`) does not match the type name the `dh:code-reviewer` agent registers (`audit-report`). The skill's follow-up handling step fails on the `artifact_read` call and falls through to the SAM search fallback, requiring the orchestrator to discover the correct type via `artifact_list` before proceeding.\\n\\nObserved: `complete-implementation` Recursive Follow-up Handling step, session 2026-05-25, issue #2437. Affected: every `complete-implementation` run that reads the code review verdict from the artifact.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **complete-implementation reads codebase-analysis artifact type for code review verdict but dh:code-reviewer registers audit-report** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation 2026-05-25 \u2014 complete-implementation run for issue #2437\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-28)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING**\\n\\nAll inputs are PRESENT from primary sources. Root cause is confirmed by direct source reading, not inference.\\n\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent (what is broken) | PRESENT | Issue #2458 description + session log 2026-05-25 |\\n| Failing call site | PRESENT | `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` line 571: `artifact_read(item_id, artifact_type=\\\"codebase-analysis\\\")` |\\n| Current agent registration | PRESENT | `code-reviewer.md` line 169: `type=\\\"codebase-analysis\\\"` \u2014 already aligned |\\n| Artifact type authority | PRESENT | `CLAUDE.md` Artifact Manifest System: both `codebase-analysis` and `audit-report` are listed as valid types |\\n| Fallback path | PRESENT | `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` lines 574\u2013578: `artifact_list` fallback emits WARNING when type differs |\\n| Fix scope | PRESENT \u2014 trivial | One-file fix to `code-reviewer.md` was already applied; verification and doc cleanup remain |\\n\\nNo invented facts. All claims sourced from file reads with line references.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n**Current state** (as of primary source review 2026-05-28): The `code-reviewer.md` agent file already registers as `codebase-analysis` (line 169). The original bug required an in-flight session with the old agent that registered `audit-report`.\\n\\nTo verify the fix is complete:\\n\\n1. Dispatch `@dh:code-reviewer` for any task with a known `item_id`\\n2. Observe the artifact registration call in agent output: `type=\\\"codebase-analysis\\\"` must appear\\n3. Run `complete-implementation` on the same task\\n4. The Recursive Follow-up Handling step must call `artifact_read(item_id, artifact_type=\\\"codebase-analysis\\\")` and receive the report without falling through to the fallback path\\n5. Confirm no `WARNING: artifact type differs` message appears in output\\n\\nFallback path (lines 574\u2013578 of `complete-implementation/SKILL.md`) can still be verified by temporarily forcing an `audit-report` registration \u2014 the fallback should emit WARNING and recover.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- **Session 2026-05-25, issue #2437**: `artifact_read(2437, \\\"codebase-analysis\\\")` returned `{\\\"error\\\": \\\"No artifacts of type 'codebase-analysis' found for item #2437\\\"}`. `artifact_list(2437)` showed registration as `artifact_type=\\\"audit-report\\\"` with `artifact_id=\\\"code-review-2437-T1\\\"`. Reading `audit-report` returned the expected `verdict` field.\\n- **Current `code-reviewer.md`**: Lines 169 and 177 confirm the fix is now in the agent file \u2014 `type=\\\"codebase-analysis\\\"` is the registered type, with `audit-report` explicitly forbidden and explained.\\n- **`complete-implementation/SKILL.md` line 571**: Consumer call unchanged \u2014 `artifact_read(item_id, artifact_type=\\\"codebase-analysis\\\")`.\\n- **`complete-implementation/SKILL.md` lines 574\u2013578**: Fallback path added post-bug \u2014 handles type mismatch via `artifact_list` + re-read + WARNING.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- `complete-implementation` reads the code review verdict reliably on the primary path without falling through to the fallback\\n- The WARNING in the fallback path becomes a true anomaly signal rather than routine noise\\n- `audit-report` type becomes exclusively owned by `dh:doc-drift-auditor` with no cross-type confusion\\n- Future `code-reviewer.md` modifications have an explicit CRITICAL warning preventing type regression\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `@dh:code-reviewer` completes a review, `complete-implementation`'s Recursive Follow-up Handling step reads the verdict via `artifact_read(item_id, artifact_type=\\\"codebase-analysis\\\")` and receives the report without error. No fallback path is needed. The artifact type `audit-report` is used only by `dh:doc-drift-auditor`.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `code-reviewer.md` registers its artifact as `type=\\\"codebase-analysis\\\"` (verified: line 169 \u2014 already done)\\n2. `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` reads the verdict via `artifact_read(item_id, artifact_type=\\\"codebase-analysis\\\")` (verified: line 571 \u2014 already done)\\n3. No occurrence of `type=\\\"audit-report\\\"` in `code-reviewer.md` (verified: grep returns no matches \u2014 already done)\\n4. The fallback path in `complete-implementation` (lines 574\u2013578) emits a WARNING when the actual type differs from `codebase-analysis` \u2014 this must remain as a regression detector\\n5. `CLAUDE.md` Artifact Manifest System section documents that `codebase-analysis` is the code reviewer type and `audit-report` is the drift auditor type, with no ambiguity\\n6. An end-to-end run of `complete-implementation` on a plan-linked issue with a NEEDS-WORK verdict from `code-reviewer` completes Phase T1 post-dispatch without the WARNING being emitted\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|---|---|\\n| Primary file | `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md` \u2014 producer; fix applied at lines 169 and 177 |\\n| Primary file | `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 consumer; Recursive Follow-up Handling step lines 570\u2013598 |\\n| Reference | `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 Artifact Manifest System section, artifact types list |\\n| Issue | #2437 \u2014 the session where the mismatch was observed (referenced in bug report) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 all required files are present and readable\\n- Blocks: None identified\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone. All inputs are present. The primary fix (code-reviewer.md alignment) is already applied. Remaining work is verification and any follow-on cleanup of CLAUDE.md artifact type documentation if it is ambiguous.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the producer-side fix (`code-reviewer.md`) is already applied. Remaining work is: (1) end-to-end verification that the fix holds, (2) confirm `CLAUDE.md` artifact type documentation is unambiguous. No code changes expected unless verification reveals a regression.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:77b91612fb1d0a6a5e54123193e3adcf -->\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nThe artifact type contract in `CLAUDE.md` (Artifact Manifest System section) lists both `codebase-analysis` and `audit-report` as valid types, with `audit-report` documented as the type for `dh:doc-drift-auditor`. The fix in `code-reviewer.md` aligns with this contract: `codebase-analysis` is the code reviewer's type; `audit-report` is the drift auditor's type.\\n\\nThe CRITICAL warning in `code-reviewer.md` (line 177) makes the contract explicit and enforcement-oriented: future agents authoring or editing `code-reviewer.md` cannot misassign the type without seeing the warning. This is the correct approach \u2014 it places the constraint at the point of production, not just at the point of consumption.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n**Blast radius: narrow but workflow-breaking.**\\n\\n- **Primary path broken**: Every `complete-implementation` run that reaches Phase T1 (Code Review) and then enters Recursive Follow-up Handling is affected. Without the correct artifact type, `artifact_read` fails and the quality gate falls through to the SAM search fallback \u2014 which may return no results, causing follow-up detection to be silently skipped.\\n- **Silent failure mode**: If the fallback SAM search also returns empty (common when no `{slug}-followup` plans exist), the skill proceeds as if there are no follow-up files \u2014 potentially suppressing real blocking findings.\\n- **Secondary path**: The fallback path (lines 574\u2013578) provides partial recovery: `artifact_list` + re-read by actual type. But it emits a WARNING rather than failing loudly, so the mismatch can go unnoticed in logs.\\n- **Scope**: Affects all users of `/complete-implementation` that use the SAM path (plan-linked issues). The PQG (proportional quality gates) path has no code review artifact read.\\n- **Downstream**: `status:verified` label could be applied to issues where blocking code review findings were missed.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**defect** \u2014 The `dh:code-reviewer` agent registered its output under the wrong artifact type (`audit-report` instead of `codebase-analysis`), causing `complete-implementation`'s `artifact_read` call to fail at the Recursive Follow-up Handling step. The consumer (`complete-implementation`) correctly expected `codebase-analysis` per the artifact type contract in CLAUDE.md, but the producer (`code-reviewer`) had registered under a different type.\\n\\nRoot cause: the artifact type contract was not enforced at the producer level. The `code-reviewer.md` has since been updated to register as `codebase-analysis` (line 169) with an explicit CRITICAL warning (line 177). The fallback path in `complete-implementation` (lines 574\u2013578) was added to handle the case where the type differs, emitting a WARNING and re-reading with the actual type.\\n\",\"digest\":\"6b84786bd9c4d7997ef41394a7c72cd3f31ca526e2be436eb739888425c50152\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCOeqg\"}"}